# R6 Round-3 (2026-10-17): line endings are gate semantics for the xp-gate
# boundary files. A CRLF line in the analysis-paths/prune-dirs lists used to
# hand the hook an entry like "references/scripts\r"; the path test failed and
# Gate 1 degraded from a real product-scope analysis to a WARN without any
# error signal. Pin LF explicitly (verified: the adapter now also strips CR,
# this is the belt-and-suspenders second layer). NOTE: eol=lf is a
# checkout-time normalization only - it does not rewrite existing blobs or
# stop a same-machine writer from putting CRLF content on disk; the adapter's
# CR stripping is the enforcing layer.
.xp-gate-powershell-analysis-paths text eol=lf
.xp-gate-powershell-prune-dirs   text eol=lf
.xp-gate-powershell-coverage-ignore text eol=lf
githooks/**                      text eol=lf
*.sh                             text eol=lf

# Markdown is read by tools/Update-DocTables.ps1, which preserves whatever
# newlines the target file already carried. Two docs were CRLF while every
# other doc was LF, so the same -Check could report differently depending on
# which file you were looking at. Pin LF so a checkout cannot reintroduce the
# split.
*.md                             text eol=lf
